{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Virginia High School, home of the Blue Devils, educates students grades 7-12 in Virginia, Minnesota.","title":"Virginia High School (Minnesota)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is a public high school with open enrollment located across from the Saint Louis County District Courthouse on scenic 5th Avenue.","title":"Virginia High School (Minnesota)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Virginia High School has a strong music department known for the Marching Blues, the school's marching band.","title":"Virginia High School (Minnesota)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The high school also participates in Minnesota State High School League sports such as hockey, basketball, volleyball, tennis, football, track & field, cross country, baseball, swimming, golf, and soccer.","title":"Virginia High School (Minnesota)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Despite budget problems in the past decade due to declining enrollment, Virginia Secondary has had success in standardized state testing, graduation rates, and school pride.","title":"Virginia High School (Minnesota)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The enrollment has been at a slow decline for the last few decades (as has the city of Virginia's population) but enrollment has been increasing in the lower grade levels.","title":"Virginia High School (Minnesota)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Virginia is a city in Saint Louis County, Minnesota, United States, on the Mesabi Iron Range.","title":"Virginia, Minnesota"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The population was 8,712 at the 2010 census.","title":"Virginia, Minnesota"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" According to a water tower in the middle of town, the city's nickname is the "Queen City", or "Queen City of the North".","title":"Virginia, Minnesota"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Over the last many decades, Redbank Valley has been known throughout the surrounding counties as prestige institution of education.","title":"Redbank Valley School District"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The Redbank Valley High School (RVHS) athletics, education, and arts programs have been recognized throughout surrounding districts and communities.","title":"Redbank Valley School District"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" RVHS's "Bulldog Marching Band" was, at one point, the No. 1 marching band in the state, competing and placing high in both the North American Marching Band Association and the Lakeshore Marching Band Association.","title":"Redbank Valley School District"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" This is followed by the fine athletic programs, that have won numerous championships across the many sports programs provided.","title":"Redbank Valley School District"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" This has spanned across not only District IX, but on the state level as well.","title":"Redbank Valley School District"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Education recently topped these all, as not even a decade ago, the school district had been educating many students that would receive highly regarded majors and doctorates.","title":"Redbank Valley School District"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Cal Poly Mustang Band, also known as The Pride of the Pacific, is the official marching band of California Polytechnic State University in the city of San Luis Obispo, California.","title":"Mustang Band"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Although the band is not a competitive marching band they serve as a school spirit organization.","title":"Mustang Band"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The band functions in two different forms throughout the year.","title":"Mustang Band"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" In the fall the band marches as The Mustang Marching Band and during Cal Poly's winter quarter they function as a pep band.","title":"Mustang Band"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The band attends many athletic events during the year to encourage the school's athletic teams and audience support/involvement.","title":"Mustang Band"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The marching band is well-known around campus as an exciting and spirited group that brings pep, passion, and tradition to every performance.","title":"Mustang Band"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The marching band is conducted by three directors: Andrew McMahan (Director of Bands), Christopher Woodruff (Associate Director), and Len Kawamoto (Assistant Director).","title":"Mustang Band"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"With over 250 members, the Oregon State University Marching Band, ("OSUMB"), is the marching band of Oregon State University, known as the ""Spirit and Sound of OSU"."","title":"Oregon State University Marching Band"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was founded in 1891 making it the oldest band in the Pac-12.","title":"Oregon State University Marching Band"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The Oregon State University Marching Band is the primary athletic band at Oregon State.","title":"Oregon State University Marching Band"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" In addition to the Oregon State University Marching Band, other athletic bands include Basketball Band, Rhythm & Beavs, Rhythm & Beavs: Travel Band, the Away Game Pep Band (for select away games), Alumni Band (the band that covers any games occurring prior to the start of the school term), Gymnastics Band (the ensemble that performs at home gymnastic meets; this ensemble also include alumni members), and Bar Band (a small ensemble that tours local bars on the day before a home football game).","title":"Oregon State University Marching Band"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" All band members are required to participate in marching band before they may be eligible to participate in any of the other bands Oregon State offers.","title":"Oregon State University Marching Band"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Bands of America (BOA), a division of Music for All, is an organization that promotes and organizes marching band competitions for high school students.","title":"Bands of America"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Competitions include both Regional and Super Regional Championships as well as the Grand National Champ